    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In developing countries, data collection can be time-consuming, outdated, and of poor quality. However, as technology advances and global networks improve, there is increased capacity and opportunity for a localized data revolution in low and middle-income countries to generate and use their own data to implement and make better decisions in health, education, and other key sectors.",
